"overview": "Massachusetts is one of the most Democratic states in the country, and Governor Maura Healey is seeking a second term with the full weight of incumbency behind her. Polling throughout 2026 has been remarkably consistent: every survey since February has shown Healey leading Republican Mike Minogue by 16 to 29 points, with the two most recent surveys in late September at +21 and +16. Aggregated estimates put the race around 19 to 20 points.\n\nMinogue, a businessman making his first statewide run, has struggled to gain traction; the Boston Globe reports his economic pitch is not resonating with voters. The campaigns have combined to spend roughly $13 million, and the first debate in early October centered on Healey's efforts to tie Minogue to Trump. All seven expert raters call the race Solid or Safe Democratic, and prediction markets price Healey's chances at about 95 percent.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9961, "margin": 18.83}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9968, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9983, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9947, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9929, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9875, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9913, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9921, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9908, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9953, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9946, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9924, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9932, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9949, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9959, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9955, "margin": 18.5}]}